{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience","id":1099098,"title":"True to tribe vs player experience","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-01T04:03:33-07:00","id":1099098,"title":"True to tribe vs player experience","content":"I am an online gamer, I have played WtA in various forms for over 4 years now. And I have read up on the logs of many other games, too.<br /> <br /> There are tribes that usually get banned, two of them which actually make me ponder the reasons why.<br /> <br /> One is naturally, the Red Talons but the other is Wendigo. Both are usually banned due to them being disruptive to the game, which has raised questions for me a lot. Please note that online games usually are multi player games with non-ST involved play.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Wendigo and Talons are seen as RARR HUMANS/WHITES and so unfit for such a larger scale game. This being true to tribal portrayal at parts, too. But to me, it always confuses me how often the players of these two tribes then go for that exact behaviour, when it is typically seen as bothersome or just tiring in the long run. Red Talon reacting once negatively can be fun, but -constantly-? Is it really fun for the player themselves to have their character basically exist as nothing but a red ball of anger? Same with Wendigo, though they at least ARE given much more depth more often than Talons.<br /> <br /> The question I am asking here is where do you guys draw the line with character behaviour versus just being tiring to other players? This doesn't have to be the aforementioned rage piles, it could be pretty much any tribal stereotype played a bit far and bit too often.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T09:18:29-07:00","id":1099180,"title":"","content":"Well, Red Talons tend to be banned because they are disruptive any game involving peaceful reactions with humans. I have never seen Wendigos banned though, as Wendigos are fighting existent racism against Native Americans (they are not happy about Whites, but they would just like the Whites to stop pissing on the Native Americans and to honor the old treaties).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T09:23:48-07:00","id":1099183,"title":"","content":"A lot of it comes down to player maturity imo. A lot of people have the preconceived notion that werewolf is all about combat and play under that mind set even after being shown it's not. <br /> <br /> I never understood the ban red talons thing, might as well ban people from playing a lupus at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:12:14-07:00","id":1099202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099183#post1099183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never understood the ban red talons thing, might as well ban people from playing a lupus at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, when I started, it was -very- common to see lupus banned outright. It has gotten a lot better, but the general mentality was that no one could play them right so why bother. Metis weren't, though, I think it was just assumed that they'd act like homids.<br /> <br /> I think Wendigo were banned also because people got worried of doing wrong by the tribe. I literally saw one game where Striders, Uktena, Wendigo and Stargazers were banned.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:06:30-07:00","id":1099254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099202#post1099202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, when I started, it was -very- common to see lupus banned outright. It has gotten a lot better, but the general mentality was that no one could play them right so why bother. Metis weren't, though, I think it was just assumed that they'd act like homids.<br /> <br /> I think Wendigo were banned also because people got worried of doing wrong by the tribe. I literally saw one game where Striders, Uktena, Wendigo and Stargazers were banned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I banned Stargazers, Wendigo and Uktena in my game... most of that though is due to forcing the players to be 'Wyrmbringers,' which was a conscious decision on my part. I didn't want anyone playing Bunyip or Stargazers either because I had already decided there weren't any members of these tribes currently running around the Southwest in 1840 after the moonbridges had failed.<br /> <br /> Are others banning them for similar reasons, or are other storytellers just not trusting their players to portray Wendigo or Talons properly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:21:50-07:00","id":1099260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099254#post1099254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I banned Stargazers, Wendigo and Uktena in my game... most of that though is due to forcing the players to be 'Wyrmbringers,' which was a conscious decision on my part. I didn't want anyone playing Bunyip or Stargazers either because I had already decided there weren't any members of these tribes currently running around the Southwest in 1840 after the moonbridges had failed.<br /> <br /> Are others banning them for similar reasons, or are other storytellers just not trusting their players to portray Wendigo or Talons properly?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, you don't have a forum with 20+ players, plus you have setting reasons to limit them.<br /> <br /> It is the latter, though. Not to mention a lot of people who pick up Talons think it is okay to play a character who constantly argues and questions elders, without really any good payoff. There was this MET guide written by a fan encouraging it, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T15:22:48-07:00","id":1099305,"title":"","content":"I'd argue there's nothing wrong with Red Talons or Wendigo.. but the sort of player who I wouldn't let play either is also the sort of player I wouldn't let play much. I mean they are just using &quot;Its just my character&quot; to justify &quot;I want to play a really disruptive character&quot;<br /> <br /> On the otherhand Larps and Chatroom setups are FUNDIMENTALLY different from simple tabletop/small games. When I run a tabletop style game even online I generally am able to dictate the culture and set up of the Garou outside the PC pack. Those 3 to 5 people can be as super snowflakey as they want because they are the only players that I have to deal with. They do not create the world. In a broad chatroom/larp though the culture of the sept(and if you are linked to other games the world) is effected by who you allow in. If you want Red Talons to be rare you may have to ban them not because they are disruptive but because they don't work with the setting, a Similar issue might occur with Wendigo they are definately conceptually tied to certain areas, I know for example a larp I was in had a very high Wendigo presence in Maryland. It came off as extremely off putting, to the point it would seem like 1 in 5 Native Americans in the state were kinfolk.<br /> <br /> So sometimes you have to put caps on tribes and sometimes its just easier to ban a tribe then deal with the 50th person who thinks they have a cool fitting concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T15:32:03-07:00","id":1099309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience#post1099098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I am asking here is where do you guys draw the line with character behaviour versus just being tiring to other players? This doesn't have to be the aforementioned rage piles, it could be pretty much any tribal stereotype played a bit far and bit too often.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my personal games, the point is for everyone to have fun. Anyone playing anything that's just grating and tiring to other players is a problem to be solved. In reality, all of the classic 'problem player' archetypes really come down to someone that's taking a tolerable or even good thing too far and/or doing it too often.<br /> <br /> I try to bring this out into bigger games like online play. I want people to have fun with my characters, so I have people to play with, so I don't want to overplay things that piss off other players. But there's also limits. If I'm playing a hard-ass by-the-books Philodox, I'm not going to have him just stop caring about other characters being careless with the rules of Garou society. I need to have fun with my character too. There's a point where you have to stand up for the integrity of your concept as well. So my line is contextual with the other people I'm playing with. Those that will cooperatively adjust to make play fun will receive adjustments from me to get everything going. Those that just want to do their thing and don't care if other people want to play with that aren't going to get me to adjust what I'm playing for their fun.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately in online play, it's a lot easier for people that get off on being the center of attention more than making sure everyone's having fun to indulge. The easier a given character type is for people to say, &quot;I'm just playing my character!&quot; the more everyone gets restriction/ban/etc. happy on them beyond any sensible things like setting rationales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:43:38-07:00","id":1099493,"title":"","content":"No one has ever wanted to play a Red Talon at my game.<br /> <br /> However, Wendigo have shown up all the time. Yeah, Wendigo are a bunch of racists against whites but that's the TRIBE versus individual players. And, bluntly, it's the rare player who doesn't think they have a point. Native Americans did get and continue to do get, the short end of the stick. In the same manner that a man on fire is slightly warm.<br /> <br /> Wendigo are also very useful as foils for, say, the Silver Fang who are racist in their own way.<br /> <br /> NPC and Player Wendigo at my table are less likely to be, &quot;Kill Whitey&quot; and more, &quot;Listen, we're trying to preserve our culture and keep our people from extermination. If that requires violence, so be it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-02-2017, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T19:57:54-07:00","id":1099728,"title":"","content":"The 'Kill Whitey' Wendigo is just another sad relic of 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T20:04:32-07:00","id":1099731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099728#post1099728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'Kill Whitey' Wendigo is just another sad relic of 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, my problem with W:TA and racial identity politics is that it's not quite a mature enough game to pull it off. Not that it's not an issue which a socially aware game like W:TA shouldn't tackle.<br /> <br /> The idea of there being white supremacist Get like the Swords of Heimdall as villains doesn't bother more unless some assheads think they have a point at my table. I also think the game was talking down to me by saying in Revised, &quot;And Oh God, we all realized RACISM IS WRONG and killed them.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T21:24:50-07:00","id":1099745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099728#post1099728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'Kill Whitey' Wendigo is just another sad relic of 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't Evan in the comic in 1e along with 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T02:14:28-07:00","id":1099780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099731#post1099731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, my problem with W:TA and racial identity politics is that it's not quite a mature enough game to pull it off. Not that it's not an issue which a socially aware game like W:TA shouldn't tackle.<br /> <br /> The idea of there being white supremacist Get like the Swords of Heimdall as villains doesn't bother more unless some assheads think they have a point at my table. I also think the game was talking down to me by saying in Revised, &quot;And Oh God, we all realized RACISM IS WRONG and killed them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>At this, I have to point out that a huge issue with the 1ed vs Revised tribebooks was that the former wrote the fenrir basically as german. While the latter actually was based more on actual nordic culture. And I think that affected that writing, because at times I see people write the Fenrir basically as all neo-nazi and all german(based). While nordic imagery is tied to nazism, the actual countries and cultures do not reflect that and even far back, didn't. Of course we do have our own neonazi groups and racial issues, but the way the 1ed did it was way off base.<br /> <br /> Plus, the book actually explains the reason why the Swords of Heimindal were destroyed as backlash from the Nation basically making the Fenrir the omega tribe. As in, they had to unpack their own racism and issues to actually be respected again. And given how my country did ally with the nazi (against the USSR, but still) and Norway was occupied, it reflects the real life issues of dealing with such a past and being the source of many imagery used by the white supremecists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T07:20:41-07:00","id":1099814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099780#post1099780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this, I have to point out that a huge issue with the 1ed vs Revised tribebooks was that the former wrote the fenrir basically as german. While the latter actually was based more on actual nordic culture. And I think that affected that writing, because at times I see people write the Fenrir basically as all neo-nazi and all german(based). While nordic imagery is tied to nazism, the actual countries and cultures do not reflect that and even far back, didn't. Of course we do have our own neonazi groups and racial issues, but the way the 1ed did it was way off base.<br /> <br /> Plus, the book actually explains the reason why the Swords of Heimindal were destroyed as backlash from the Nation basically making the Fenrir the omega tribe. As in, they had to unpack their own racism and issues to actually be respected again. And given how my country did ally with the nazi (against the USSR, but still) and Norway was occupied, it reflects the real life issues of dealing with such a past and being the source of many imagery used by the white supremacists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of a larger issue in Werewolf: The Apocalypse itself in that 12 tribes of mostly European people are supposed to cover the entirety of the human race's various cultures. One of the things I liked about Rage across Russia was the fact they simply said, &quot;No, that's not how it works at all. Every single country in the world, generally, has its own branches of the tribes.&quot; It's not perfect but I generally think it's better than the alternative that we don't have any sort of diversity whatsoever with the Garou.<br /> <br /> Which gets back to the issue of the Swords of Heimdall with the fact the whole Germans=Nazis thing is awful and I would never want to perpetuate that B.S. nor limit the Get of Fenris to being THE German tribe which wouldn't make any damn sense anyway since that would mean they'd be the English Tribe as well. Also, if they WERE the Scandinavian tribe they'd be the rulers of the English tribe and the Russians AND the Germans. The Silver Fangs, honestly, as depicted should be the Nordic tribe if Werewolf was historical. The Get of Fenris suffer from being the &quot;Theme Park&quot; version of Vikings so we never get to see the explorer or trader aspects of them but just the berserker.<br /> <br /> But the issue is if you're going to deal with racism as a theme in the game I think it's a good thing to have the people who are there to be dealt with. The Garou practice racism as an undeniable part of their culture because it's a game about bloodlines, heritage, and long simmering ethnic conflicts. I came in with 2nd Edition but the opening comic and poor Evan (who no one respects) told me a major theme of the game was going to be, &quot;You are going to try to heal the conflicts which the Garou have in their past.&quot; Native Americans, Whites, Aborigines (the Bunyip should still be alive), Croaton, and class issues. It's a game where one of the flaws of the Garou is they have to learn to get along and i think it's a richer game for it.<br /> <br /> The SoH were guys you were supposed to claw anyway but I was annoyed by their destruction because it deprives a group of people who are obvious bad guys to say the awful stuff needed. Albeit, I wouldn't have kept them as Nazis but maybe rewritten them as the faction which is more generically about keeping Get lines &quot;pure&quot; and talking smack about other tribes as well as how the War of Rage was a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-03-2017, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:26:18-07:00","id":1099864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099814#post1099814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's sort of a larger issue in Werewolf: The Apocalypse itself in that 12 tribes of mostly European people are supposed to cover the entirety of the human race's various cultures. One of the things I liked about Rage across Russia was the fact they simply said, &quot;No, that's not how it works at all. Every single country in the world, generally, has its own branches of the tribes.&quot; It's not perfect but I generally think it's better than the alternative that we don't have any sort of diversity whatsoever with the Garou.<br /> <br /> Which gets back to the issue of the Swords of Heimdall with the fact the whole Germans=Nazis thing is awful and I would never want to perpetuate that B.S. nor limit the Get of Fenris to being THE German tribe which wouldn't make any damn sense anyway since that would mean they'd be the English Tribe as well. Also, if they WERE the Scandinavian tribe they'd be the rulers of the English tribe and the Russians AND the Germans. The Silver Fangs, honestly, as depicted should be the Nordic tribe if Werewolf was historical. The Get of Fenris suffer from being the &quot;Theme Park&quot; version of Vikings so we never get to see the explorer or trader aspects of them but just the berserker.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the issues with WtA has been that the 2nd ed went WAY over the top with the tribes. Sure, the 1st ed wasn't exactly flowery, but 1st ed Black Furies and 2nd ed Furies for example are basically two different tribes by mentality.<br /> <br /> For the Fenrir, they weren't vikings, as in WoD the norse gods were their foes. But still, when the setting was planned, the imagery of neonazism was stuck on them like being drunks was for the Fianna. The writers of the revised TB had to basically make reverse engineer the tribe at parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099098-true-to-tribe-vs-player-experience?p=1099814#post1099814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The SoH were guys you were supposed to claw anyway but I was annoyed by their destruction because it deprives a group of people who are obvious bad guys to say the awful stuff needed. Albeit, I wouldn't have kept them as Nazis but maybe rewritten them as the faction which is more generically about keeping Get lines &quot;pure&quot; and talking smack about other tribes as well as how the War of Rage was a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every tribe in a sense has a faction like that, but instead of the Fenrir, I'd say Silver Fangs would be the better tribe to use for racial purity and such themes. The Fenrir got that label because the stereotype of the neonazi was a germanic person, or a nordic one. But Silver Fangs to me personally feel a great representation of how effed up people who want lines actually pure can be.<br /> <br /> Plus, these days the racial purists are educated looking people, plus you can always throw in the dog breeding world's nastiness on keeping their breeds pure even as they are falling apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:27:38-07:00","id":1099866,"title":"","content":"I would not mind a retcon of having the Swords of Heimdell having fallen to the Wyrm during World War II and having joined the Black Spiral Dancers after the Nazi defeat of WW II. I am not sure if the Silver Fangs should care about racial purity, as Pure Breed is also a spiritual trait. If a Silver Fang Kinfolk marries a black woman and their child is born with a spiritual connection to the Silver Fangs, what would they care? And there are supposed to be Silver Fangs throughout Asia, so they are not really a European Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 06-03-2017, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}